<title>POLAND: Kable falls 9.8 pct on low tender offer.</title>
<headline>Kable falls 9.8 pct on low tender offer.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish cable maker Kable SA fell 9.8 percent to 36 zlotys after 25-percent owner NKT Cables' mid-week announcement of public tender offers to buy up the firm at 27.9 zlotys per share, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;The lower price apparently had a psychological effect,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Analysts also said Kable's surges earlier this month after the Danish firm had announced it planned to gain a majority share already discounted the potential takeover. Analysts saw the stock now stabilising.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
